#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087394 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cfc862ea-961c-50e4-a89b-10c5ef88d851" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "08a55503-97c4-5987-8c97-71990b6c2cbc" :question/math-academy-id "e-3220" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $x^2 + y^2 = 9$?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2=9\n$$\n\nrepresents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{2} &= 9 \\\\\nr &= \\sqrt{9} \\\\\nr &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nIn conclusion, the circle is centered at the origin and its radius is $3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087395 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31d92381-0c28-53fc-b918-99c16544c201" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "5382cb24-6a11-51a5-bc80-5cfed0412870" :question/math-academy-id "e-3221" :question/problem "What is the equation of the circle given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/842/Source/Images/b8d596fae077045562ff9917b3557fa7.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and has radius $r = 2$. So, the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 2^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087396 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "30bb1401-f704-520c-a23e-5a238e44960e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "f7713cee-abb9-5ac6-bf69-7ddc7c14e3fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-3223" :question/problem "Which equation describes the set of all points $(x,y)$ in the coordinate plane that are a distance of $4$ from the origin?" :question/worked-solution "The set of all points $(x,y)$ that are a distance $4$ from the origin defines a circle with radius $r=4$ centered at the origin, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/842/Source/Images/18f2f791e40fb242e0ab6db9f5bd4a70.png)\n\nSo, the required equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 4^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087398 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e75012ec-8203-574b-ba07-0a26e4cf4691" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/id #uuid "4a9af9d3-13b3-5510-a46e-5babac13cd40" :question/math-academy-id "e-3225" :question/problem "Given that the points $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(-2,4)$ and $(2,-4)$, respectively, lie on a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/842/Source/Images/3342ece562d34274187b008c4c1fbdbe.png)" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r$, centered at the origin, is\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nNow, we first calculate the diameter $AB$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{(-2 - 2)^{2} + (4 - (-4))^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + 8^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16 + 64} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{80} \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overline{AB}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{AB}{2} = \\dfrac {4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt5\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= (2\\sqrt{5})^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} + y^{2} &= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cfc862ea-961c-50e4-a89b-10c5ef88d851" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "811d23e4-6715-5da7-a123-94aca7f234aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086444} {:answer/id #uuid "139e7954-fc75-5de3-8292-f36d85c2a064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{10}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086445} {:answer/id #uuid "2137b558-4293-561c-a163-e118d35ba77a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2, 2)$ and radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086446} {:answer/id #uuid "29b868ad-04ec-5ed8-afe0-2c4ef7f2f0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2, 2)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{10}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086447} {:answer/id #uuid "54c77a24-d3b2-5bd7-a01e-4f85b8765a2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "139e7954-fc75-5de3-8292-f36d85c2a064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{10}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086445} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b9d3c3-c9b4-54f6-8cc9-fd18d2edaeed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086443}] :question/id #uuid "3c03b867-7bb8-5ab7-b225-6c4b9c7f1dfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-7509" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $x^{2} + y^{2} = 10$?"}]}
